/// @class superdex::robotics::SensorBase
///
/// @brief Base class for robot sensors. Derives from ComponentBase for common lifecycle (validity, actor, destroy). Each derived sensor keeps its own specialized ComputeSignal signature.
///

/// @fn TransformRT const& superdex::robotics::SensorBase::GetParentFromSensor() const
///
/// @brief The sensor's pose relative to its parent frame: the associated link's actor for bot-owned sensors, or the scene root for scene-level / actor-less sensors. aFromB convention (maps sensor-frame coordinates into the parent frame).
///
/// @return Sensor pose relative to its parent frame.
///

/// @fn void superdex::robotics::SensorBase::SetParentFromSensor(TransformRT const& parentFromSensor)
///
/// @brief Set the sensor's pose relative to its parent frame.
///
/// @param[in] parentFromSensor The new parent-from-sensor transform (aFromB convention).
///

/// @fn TransformRT superdex::robotics::SensorBase::GetWorldTransform() const
///
/// @brief The sensor's pose in world space. When the sensor is bound to a Mochi @ref mochi::Actor "Actor", that actor's transform is already world-resolved by the simulation, so world = actorWorldTransform * parentFromSensor. When the sensor has no actor (a fusion sensor that consumes other sensors, or a scene sensor standing in for a scene root that has no Mochi actor), the scene root is the parent: world = parentFromSensor, i.e. the scene-root-to-world transform is treated as identity (a surrogate for a real scene-root actor) until scene spawn transforms are supported.
///
/// @return Sensor pose in world space.
///

/// @class superdex::robotics::ActuatorBase
///
/// @brief Base class for robot actuators.
///
/// Mirrors @ref superdex::robotics::ControllerBase "ControllerBase" and @ref superdex::robotics::SensorBase "SensorBase": derives from ComponentBase for common lifecycle (validity, actor, destroy). No concrete actuators exist yet; this establishes the contract early so the first actuator follows the same shape as controllers and sensors.
///
/// Registration contract (a `RoboticsContext::RegisterActuator<T>` template lands with the first concrete actuator, mirroring RegisterController/RegisterSensor): every actuator must declare static constexpr std::string_view TypeName() { return "..."; } (used by the registration templates and for the generated Python type_name() binding), implement std::string_view GetTypeName() const override; // returns TypeName() and provide a uniform constructor ActuatorX(Actor* actor, std::string_view paramArgs, Error& error); that loads its own params from the path or inline JSON. An (Actor*, Params const&, Error&) overload is recommended for programmatic / non-filesystem construction.
///
/// Teardown contract (mirrors @ref superdex::robotics::ControllerBase "ControllerBase" / @ref superdex::robotics::SensorBase "SensorBase"): @ref superdex::robotics::ComponentBase::GetActor "GetActor" resolves the live actor on demand and yields None once the owning mochi Scene (or the actor) is gone, so an actuator that outlives its Scene (Scene destroyed before the RoboticsContext) sees @ref superdex::robotics::ComponentBase::GetActor "GetActor" == None in its destructor. Any concrete actuator whose destructor releases actor-held resources must therefore guard on GetActor() != None (or, for context-owned resources, resolve via GetContext()) so teardown never dereferences a dangling Actor*.
///

/// @class superdex::robotics::CameraSensor
///
/// @brief Camera sensor runtime object. Stores intrinsics/extrinsics for use by renderers (UE, etc.). No ComputeSignal — cameras don't produce data in the mochi physics loop; renderers query GetParams() to configure their camera actors.
///

/// @fn std::string_view superdex::robotics::CameraSensor::TypeName()
///
/// @brief Registration type name for this sensor (see RoboticsContext::RegisterSensorType).
///
/// @return This sensor's registration type name.
///

/// @fn CameraSensorParams const& superdex::robotics::CameraSensor::GetParams() const
///
/// @brief Get sensor parameters.
///
/// @return The params.
///

/// @fn void superdex::robotics::CameraSensor::SetParams(CameraSensorParams const& params, superdex::Error& error)
///
/// @brief Set sensor parameters.
///
/// @param[in] params Params.
/// @param[in,out] error Error status. Check @ref mochi::Error::IsOK "Error::IsOK" for success.
///
